TRADEMARK

Marks owned: the word Actio within the Lumofy lockup, the seal, the Arabic form
of the name, and the phrase "Feedback that closes."

How the name is presented: Actio always appears with the Lumofy house mark in
commercial contexts. The house mark is what distinguishes the product name from
unrelated marks in adjacent software categories. Actio is a proper noun. It is
never pluralised, used as a verb, made possessive, or combined with another word
to form a new name.

Permitted to third parties:
  - Stating that a product integrates with Lumofy Actio.
  - Using the horizontal lockup unmodified, with correct clear space as defined
    in logo/README.md.

Not permitted:
  - Use of the seal alone.
  - Incorporation of the name into another product name or domain.
  - Modification of any mark, including recolouring, rotation, stretching,
    outlining, adding a container or filling the aperture.
  - Application of any mark to merchandise.
  - Any implication of endorsement.

Attribution: where a third party reproduces a mark, the accompanying text reads
"Actio and the Actio seal are marks of Lumofy."

Enquiries: requests to use a mark outside these terms are directed to the brand
owner at Lumofy before any material is produced.

These terms may be revised at any time, and use of the assets constitutes
acceptance of the current version. Nothing here constitutes legal advice.
